# Event-Driven Flask Application with Jenkins, Cloud Run & Pub/Sub

## Project Overview

This project demonstrates the deployment of a Python Flask application using Jenkins CI/CD, Docker, Google Cloud Run, and Pub/Sub.

The application is designed to showcase modern DevOps and Cloud practices, including automated build, testing, containerization, and serverless deployment.

## Technologies Used

- Python
- Flask
- Jenkins
- Docker
- Google Cloud Run
- Google Cloud Pub/Sub
- GitHub
- Git

## Project Architecture

```text
GitHub
   │
   ▼
Jenkins Pipeline
   │
   ├── Build Application
   ├── Run Tests
   ├── Build Docker Image
   ├── Push Docker Image
   └── Deploy to Cloud Run
                │
                ▼
          Flask Application
                │
                ▼
            Pub/Sub
                │
                ▼
       Asynchronous Processing
```

## Features

- Flask Web Application
- CI/CD Pipeline using Jenkins
- Docker Containerization
- Automated Deployment
- Serverless Hosting with Cloud Run
- Event-Driven Architecture with Pub/Sub

## Project Structure

```text
flask-cloudrun-pubsub/
│
├── app.py
├── requirements.txt
├── Dockerfile
├── Jenkinsfile
└── README.md
```

## Learning Objectives

- Understand CI/CD concepts
- Learn Jenkins Pipeline automation
- Deploy applications using Cloud Run
- Work with Docker containers
- Implement Pub/Sub messaging
- Build cloud-native applications

